      "html": "<p>An EV charge point install must meet BS 7671. It must meet any grant scheme rules too. It must satisfy an insurer or homeowner years later. The key is the earthing and PEN fault protection. Record the RCD type, load management and tests as evidence.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>An EV charge point install is notifiable electrical work under Part P in England and Wales. BS 7671 has a section for EV charging.</li><li>PEN fault protection is the main safety issue on most TN-C-S supplies.</li><li>Record the earthing, RCD type, load management and tests, with photos.</li><li>Quickler records what the installer says and photographs. It does not decide the earthing design.</li><li>The installer signs the certificate. Quickler does not replace it.</li></ul>"
    },
