      "heading": "PEN fault protection and earthing",
      "html": "<p>On a TN-C-S (PME) supply, an open-PEN fault can put dangerous voltage on the car and the casing. BS 7671 asks you to guard against it. Usually the charge point has open-PEN detection, or you use another earthing method, such as an earth electrode.</p><p>The record must say which method you used. Quickler asks for the supply earthing, the method and the RCD type. It asks for photos of the consumer unit, charge point and electrode. You decide the design, to the current BS 7671.</p>"
